#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:1
msgid "Release 2.25.0 (2024-11-07)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:3
msgid ""
"New environment variables to override XDG locations [\\#11351](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11351)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:5
msgid "Added new environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:7
msgid "`NIX_CACHE_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:8
msgid "`NIX_CONFIG_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:9
msgid "`NIX_DATA_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:10
msgid "`NIX_STATE_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:12
msgid ""
"Each, if defined, takes precedence over the corresponding [XDG environment "
"variable](../command-ref/env-common.md#xdg-base-directories). This provides "
"more fine-grained control over where Nix looks for files. It allows having a "
"stand-alone Nix environment that only uses files in a specific directory and "
"that doesn't interfere with the user environment."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:15
msgid ""
"Define integer overflow in the Nix language as an error [\\#10968](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10968) [\\#11188](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/11188)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:17
msgid ""
"Previously, integer overflow in the Nix language invoked C++ level signed "
"overflow, which manifested as wrapping around on overflow. It now looks like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:24
msgid "Some other overflows were fixed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:25
msgid ""
"`builtins.fromJSON` of values greater than the maximum representable value "
"in a signed 64-bit integer will generate an error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:26
msgid ""
"`nixConfig` in flakes will no longer accept negative values for "
"configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:28
msgid ""
"The `build-hook` setting no longer has a useful default when using "
"`libnixstore` as a library [\\#11178](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/11178)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:30
msgid ""
"_This is an obscure issue that only affects usage of the `libnixstore` "
"library outside of the Nix executable. It is unrelated to the `post-build-"
"hook` settings, which is often used for pushing to a cache._"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:32
msgid ""
"As part the ongoing [rewrite of the build system](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/2503) to use [Meson](https://mesonbuild.com/), we are also "
"switching to packaging individual Nix components separately (and building "
"them in separate derivations). This means that when building `libnixstore` "
"we do not know where the Nix binaries will be installed --- `libnixstore` "
"doesn't know about downstream consumers like the Nix binaries at all."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:35
msgid ""
"This has a small adverse affect on remote building --- the `build-remote` "
"executable that is specified from the [`build-hook`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-build-hook) setting will not be gotten from the (presumed) "
"installation location, but instead looked up on the `PATH`. This means that "
"other applications linking `libnixstore` that wish to use remote building "
"must arrange for the `nix` command to be on the PATH (or manually overriding "
"`build-hook`) in order for that to work."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:38
msgid ""
"Long term we don't envision this being a downside, because we plan to [get "
"rid of `build-remote` and the build hook setting entirely](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/1221). There should simply be no need to have an extra, "
"intermediate layer of remote-procedure-calling when we want to connect to a "
"remote builder. The build hook protocol did in principle support custom ways "
"of remote building, but that can also be accomplished with a custom service "
"for the ssh or daemon/ssh-ng protocols, or with a custom [store type](../"
"store/types/index.md) i.e. `Store` subclass. <!-- we normally don't mention "
"classes, but consider that this release note is about a library use case -->"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:42
msgid ""
"The Perl bindings no longer expose `getBinDir` either, since the underlying "
"C++ libraries those bindings wrap no longer know the location of installed "
"binaries as described above."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:44
msgid ""
"Wrap filesystem exceptions more correctly [\\#11378](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/11378)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:46
msgid ""
"With the switch to `std::filesystem` in different places, Nix started to "
"throw `std::filesystem::filesystem_error` in many places instead of its own "
"exceptions. As a result, Nix no longer generated error traces when (for "
"example) listing a non-existing directory. It could also lead to crashes "
"inside the Nix REPL."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:49
msgid ""
"This version catches these types of exception correctly and wraps them into "
"Nix's own exception type."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:51
msgid "Author: [**@Mic92**](https://github.com/Mic92)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:53
msgid ""
"Add setting `fsync-store-paths` [\\#1218](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/1218) [\\#7126](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/7126)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:55
msgid ""
"Nix now has a setting `fsync-store-paths` that ensures that new store paths "
"are durably written to disk before they are registered as \"valid\" in Nix's "
"database. This can prevent Nix store corruption if the system crashes or "
"there is a power loss. This setting defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:57
msgid "Author: [**@squalus**](https://github.com/squalus)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:59
msgid ""
"Removing the default argument passed to the `nix fmt` formatter [\\#11438]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11438)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:61
msgid ""
"The underlying formatter no longer receives the \".\" default argument when "
"`nix fmt` is called with no arguments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:63
msgid ""
"This change was necessary as the formatter wasn't able to distinguish "
"between a user wanting to format the current folder with `nix fmt .` or the "
"generic `nix fmt`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:67
msgid ""
"The default behavior is now the responsibility of the formatter itself, and "
"allows tools such as `treefmt` to format the whole tree instead of only the "
"current directory and below."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:71
msgid "Author: [**@zimbatm**](https://github.com/zimbatm)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:73
msgid ""
"`<nix/fetchurl.nix>` uses TLS verification [\\#11585](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/11585)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:75
msgid ""
"Previously `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` did not do TLS verification. This was "
"because the Nix sandbox in the past did not have access to TLS certificates, "
"and Nix checks the hash of the fetched file anyway. However, this can expose "
"authentication data from `netrc` and URLs to man-in-the-middle attackers. In "
"addition, Nix now in some cases (such as when using impure derivations) does "
"_not_ check the hash. Therefore we have now enabled TLS verification. This "
"means that downloads by `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` will now fail if you're "
"fetching from a HTTPS server that does not have a valid certificate."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.25.md:77
msgid ""
"`<nix/fetchurl.nix>` is also known as the builtin derivation builder "
"`builtin:fetchurl`. It's not to be confused with the evaluation-time "
"function `builtins.fetchurl`, which was not affected by this issue."
msgstr ""

